[{:db/id "q-3615/selection/4e1f31b3486caeb7566e72cb5db7798fab8687c60b0fb88bb318b8c1cda61a5f" :answer/id #uuid "0b3faeb1-f4ef-52b9-89c6-69902cf18d33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615/selection/86aa1e2702c92197ba04f4674fb6f319c092fbed204f56f238b20f309d63f357" :answer/id #uuid "8096737b-b3ed-5d19-93e6-aef7bf70d66a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615/selection/89a34971eaacbaa3f54e8712589e04a4e962611d95cc3cec1ebf10f6be5380f4" :answer/id #uuid "d59685b8-c6c4-5989-a41d-30bdd1f251df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615/selection/f8000da629d1e205f2b6f05e9c438b516ef9673be9a4c4290382bf07c5141305" :answer/id #uuid "c0b453c0-81cc-5521-bd9e-9f51f1f11721" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615/selection/87ec18cd00412883dd3b3d8ad36dd3baaedc0f8c92dcfa3ea9f921c4111e271e" :answer/id #uuid "89f31892-3807-598f-9dbb-13ba441d6917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aace1bc0-4029-56bd-83f2-c490e8c58495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3615/selection/86aa1e2702c92197ba04f4674fb6f319c092fbed204f56f238b20f309d63f357" :answer-field/choices ["q-3615/selection/4e1f31b3486caeb7566e72cb5db7798fab8687c60b0fb88bb318b8c1cda61a5f" "q-3615/selection/86aa1e2702c92197ba04f4674fb6f319c092fbed204f56f238b20f309d63f357" "q-3615/selection/89a34971eaacbaa3f54e8712589e04a4e962611d95cc3cec1ebf10f6be5380f4" "q-3615/selection/f8000da629d1e205f2b6f05e9c438b516ef9673be9a4c4290382bf07c5141305" "q-3615/selection/87ec18cd00412883dd3b3d8ad36dd3baaedc0f8c92dcfa3ea9f921c4111e271e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3615" :question/id #uuid "bb88ac70-729c-5c15-8fad-c3a30aa15d49" :question/math-academy-id "q-3615" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD=(-2)^{2}-4(1)(3)=-8<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-3 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get  $A=\\frac{3}{2},$ $B=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and $C=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nNow we integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration only at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-2x+3.$ Then $(2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-2x+3| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-3615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection/e79a789916ec6b8e74195acab102ab16ffba8642685c60cf6f06d59a409bbc1a" :answer/id #uuid "d566978b-f262-5a4e-ad6f-2d7f8dfe7791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection/0aefa180c23a8671f76f2c3055edf2161e9a1a7191e1e9cc8a5628c87be89e39" :answer/id #uuid "e5e98ebc-02bd-54b5-a757-d065e8851467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+1\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection/1ee5565ae31e18281b446e9781f2e6af094536d012489b42cef7c4b5b805c136" :answer/id #uuid "27c16c28-2efc-5404-8a79-de11da720c93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection/bbe44eae95fc34315461e1df7e6685c89ab16752e1e80e7cc2ee66f3d241ea93" :answer/id #uuid "5eb240ef-bc86-5d2c-981e-a1a0eb5dfad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection/ba161276fa9481f9333cbd022619623316dc54af177645c21afb804e77b2ab02" :answer/id #uuid "a302ec84-8b84-57a3-bfde-e52507cab31d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3bfb3e0-02eb-584b-b143-02af187f4a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11357/selection/e79a789916ec6b8e74195acab102ab16ffba8642685c60cf6f06d59a409bbc1a" :answer-field/choices ["q-11357/selection/e79a789916ec6b8e74195acab102ab16ffba8642685c60cf6f06d59a409bbc1a" "q-11357/selection/0aefa180c23a8671f76f2c3055edf2161e9a1a7191e1e9cc8a5628c87be89e39" "q-11357/selection/1ee5565ae31e18281b446e9781f2e6af094536d012489b42cef7c4b5b805c136" "q-11357/selection/bbe44eae95fc34315461e1df7e6685c89ab16752e1e80e7cc2ee66f3d241ea93" "q-11357/selection/ba161276fa9481f9333cbd022619623316dc54af177645c21afb804e77b2ab02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11357" :question/id #uuid "9debd0df-2771-5276-9781-4c4c107557fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11357" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+7$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+7)(x+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+17 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-1,B=3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}=\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use a substitution $u={x}^{2}+7.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+7| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection/aef15a9e3064822918333488489e6e8f131bab0987409e005f6edcc3718a1e0d" :answer/id #uuid "60a42eec-a246-5362-b524-6ca583c5aa2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection/cfa3fa7681d31b482e3ab74cc5f085f0e868bee0c64db0f5745df0b130edf299" :answer/id #uuid "005d3e0f-d3f5-5419-8f5d-7a5989ee0002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection/9556598d9c8393609f726bf3ce884e37edb942e472bc2fe378a6c1e043913637" :answer/id #uuid "361a06f0-d2c9-5cf7-bc54-13df424db387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection/6deff16a0e65ad0a76c4c9520cce3f853014aa974958de12e9de12f7bb48d0d0" :answer/id #uuid "f7de5944-ca6c-5936-b830-3186d1191883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2({x}^{2}-4x-3)}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection/9f79ba78f50a4e51d72ce6bcddb9fb294ff25415808324e5a3bf871e9d844d61" :answer/id #uuid "bbc39e85-8e72-5152-9358-6ff1ac3cd0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aad8a85d-a67d-5b0d-85f4-b57b947ee73c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83367/selection/9f79ba78f50a4e51d72ce6bcddb9fb294ff25415808324e5a3bf871e9d844d61" :answer-field/choices ["q-83367/selection/aef15a9e3064822918333488489e6e8f131bab0987409e005f6edcc3718a1e0d" "q-83367/selection/cfa3fa7681d31b482e3ab74cc5f085f0e868bee0c64db0f5745df0b130edf299" "q-83367/selection/9556598d9c8393609f726bf3ce884e37edb942e472bc2fe378a6c1e043913637" "q-83367/selection/6deff16a0e65ad0a76c4c9520cce3f853014aa974958de12e9de12f7bb48d0d0" "q-83367/selection/9f79ba78f50a4e51d72ce6bcddb9fb294ff25415808324e5a3bf871e9d844d61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83367" :question/id #uuid "e5fc9280-fa79-5c2f-95ea-95a92d8c6c5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-83367" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(-4)^{2}-4(1)(-3)=28\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{28}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-3x-9=A({x}^{2}-4x-3)+(Bx+C)(x+3)\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=1$ and $C=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-4x-3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2(x-2)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83367/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection/9f115e528bd26780cbc9c7efe67939663566f644c93301d8895d47f612d6676d" :answer/id #uuid "d5015d66-9cb8-5042-b24a-739c400c11e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection/b43304b12ae13139383a61d1f9c7de570ea745e7364ba6444649229bf5efef29" :answer/id #uuid "1c444fcc-2f83-52bf-ae5f-99d3c3e3b388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection/e4347cd5c9a6405f8cf02ff1ebd0139df610fe6a996477534152e2fa22d3bcb7" :answer/id #uuid "9a12247b-8a10-5efa-9c8f-0f464114e935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection/bcb22e197de5afe65584599adebd392f41e09fd678bb73c5929d4a52afd86a6c" :answer/id #uuid "f376ef23-3066-5780-8a61-5fbc84f4c633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection/ffce92569d3afc970d70f558ae230390e886bc2bd659a0e78c2c4ff844eaa0d2" :answer/id #uuid "e97a06ab-412f-56dd-af2a-09333c17849a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80ec4059-883c-5d8c-94b5-eb3aeb5102dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115686/selection/b43304b12ae13139383a61d1f9c7de570ea745e7364ba6444649229bf5efef29" :answer-field/choices ["q-115686/selection/9f115e528bd26780cbc9c7efe67939663566f644c93301d8895d47f612d6676d" "q-115686/selection/b43304b12ae13139383a61d1f9c7de570ea745e7364ba6444649229bf5efef29" "q-115686/selection/e4347cd5c9a6405f8cf02ff1ebd0139df610fe6a996477534152e2fa22d3bcb7" "q-115686/selection/bcb22e197de5afe65584599adebd392f41e09fd678bb73c5929d4a52afd86a6c" "q-115686/selection/ffce92569d3afc970d70f558ae230390e886bc2bd659a0e78c2c4ff844eaa0d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115686" :question/id #uuid "99798b4d-8a0a-5c2b-888b-3cedc5021d58" :question/math-academy-id "q-115686" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+1$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{C}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+1)(x-4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-9x+5 & =(Ax+B)(x-4)+C({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=-1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection/b285d7135082201129dcedef26821de8c5c2a63e3c358012bdb8fe81035c9cf7" :answer/id #uuid "367e2e6e-aa98-522f-8acb-9b4997e4dbe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection/4e96b80c75f9f37ccad1fe56f40d7b3e1a9fdf2d53dc2d3d1d5a33776ad7a01f" :answer/id #uuid "2026753c-2a95-516a-8e36-a8b45a756c70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection/1be9fcbe2a618fbace391764b179985aba27dfe12ff75893e0941e640f163519" :answer/id #uuid "63df8e8a-de87-5f04-94ba-1adeaa275a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection/73274e74628da4c082659d78708081a9a095d9f1e6b78d0f478109b115f840e1" :answer/id #uuid "68de0c6b-840f-50fe-8dfa-9a0944c1edb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection/de122a431ffd96ac740057bbaccca99f49412ea4f4a11a7a0b760cd26b4f5230" :answer/id #uuid "f320924a-a119-5145-bb90-6cd098e55ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75d6192b-2fda-552b-b654-d948c73582f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115710/selection/73274e74628da4c082659d78708081a9a095d9f1e6b78d0f478109b115f840e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-115710/selection/b285d7135082201129dcedef26821de8c5c2a63e3c358012bdb8fe81035c9cf7" "q-115710/selection/4e96b80c75f9f37ccad1fe56f40d7b3e1a9fdf2d53dc2d3d1d5a33776ad7a01f" "q-115710/selection/1be9fcbe2a618fbace391764b179985aba27dfe12ff75893e0941e640f163519" "q-115710/selection/73274e74628da4c082659d78708081a9a095d9f1e6b78d0f478109b115f840e1" "q-115710/selection/de122a431ffd96ac740057bbaccca99f49412ea4f4a11a7a0b760cd26b4f5230"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115710" :question/id #uuid "a13ff449-7069-519d-95f0-893e15f21aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115710" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral  $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(4)^{2}-4(1)(-6)=40\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{40}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}+4x-6),$ and we get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+12x-12=A({x}^{2}+4x-6)+(Bx+C)x\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=2$, and $C=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4x-6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x+4)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115710/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
